{#
Settings → Security, first card: changing your own password.

Above the two-factor card and not inside it, because they are peers rather than
one subject with two halves — the rule settings/index.html.twig states for when
a section splits. It comes first because it is the one every account has: the
second factor is optional and most installs never switch it on, while a password
is what every single person here signs in with.

Accepts:
    passwordForm  a ChangePasswordType view, from ChangePasswordFormFactory

`padded`, like the profile card: this body is a bare form rather than a list
that pads its own rows.

The form posts as a Turbo Stream (`data-turbo-stream`) and the reply replaces
the <div id="settings-password"> this sits inside — see
PasswordController::streamResponse(). It must NOT be `data-turbo="false"`: that
would navigate to the endpoint, and the endpoint answers with a stream fragment
rather than a page.
#}
{% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
    heading:    'settings.password.heading'|trans,
    subheading: 'settings.password.subheading'|trans,
    padded:     true,
} %}
    {% block body %}
        <div class="max-w-md">
            {{ form_start(passwordForm, { attr: { 'data-turbo-stream': true } }) }}
                {{ form_widget(passwordForm) }}

                <button type="submit"
                        class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center justify-center h-9 px-4 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium
                               text-accent-ink bg-accent hover:bg-accent-strong active:bg-blue-800
                               focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent focus-visible:ring-offset-1
                               transition-colors duration-100">
                    {{ 'settings.password.submit'|trans }}
                </button>
            {{ form_end(passwordForm) }}

            <p class="mt-4 text-[11px] text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info mr-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                {{ 'settings.password.remember_me_note'|trans }}
            </p>
        </div>
    {% endblock %}
{% endembed %}
